  "chapterSummary": "Poverty is a major economic and social challenge involving inadequate command over basic necessities and wider deprivations. The poverty line identifies monetary poverty, while multidimensional approaches capture several forms of deprivation. Poverty is influenced by unemployment, unequal resources, low productivity, poor access to education and health, social exclusion and vulnerability to shocks. India has reduced poverty under several measures, but uneven development and persistent deprivation keep poverty a continuing policy challenge.",
